;; EF-4 Phase 6: a session PROTOCOL DESCRIPTOR (Send/Recv/Choose/Branch/Rec/
;; Timeout) is a type-level construct, not a runtime value -- a value is always
;; a `Session[P]`, and a descriptor is only meaningful nested inside
;; `(Session ...)`.  So a bare descriptor field is permanently rejected (unlike
;; the value-carrying `Session`/`project`/`Role` heads, which lower in EF-4).
;; See docs/archive/history/structdef-exotic-field-forms-plan.md.

(defstruct Bad [s : (Send int Close)])

(defn main [] : int 0)
